quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  5,83,"When they listen to what has been revealed to the Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him), you see their eyes overflowing with tears because of the truth they recognise. They say: ‘Our Lord! We believe, so write us down among the witnesses.’"
  5,84,Why should we not believe in Allah and the truth that has come to us? And we long for our Lord to include us in the company of the righteous people.
  5,85,"So Allah rewarded them for what they said, with Gardens with rivers flowing beneath them, to abide in them forever. That is the reward of the virtuously excellent."
  5,86,But those who disbelieve and deny Our revelations—such shall be the inhabitants of the Hellfire.
  5,87,"O believers! Do not prohibit the good things Allah has made lawful for you, and do not transgress. Indeed, Allah does not like the transgressors."
  5,88,Eat from the lawful and pure things Allah has provided you and be conscious of Allah in Whom you (all) believe.
  5,89,"Allah does not call you to account for what is frivolous in your oaths, but He will hold you accountable for your deliberate oaths. The atonement for it (i.e. the breaking of an oath) is feeding ten poor persons the average food you would normally serve to your own family, or their clothing, or freeing a slave. And whosoever does not find (the means) shall fast for three days. That is the atonement for your oaths when you have sworn (them). But guard your oaths. Thus, Allah makes clear to you His revelations so that you may be grateful."
